  "body": "## What was wrong\n\nA single 429 could hold a request for ~100 seconds before the fallback chain was ever consulted, and four env vars could only be changed by hand-editing `~/.fcc/.env`.\n\n`providers/rate_limit.py` computes `delay = min(base * 2^attempt, max) + jitter` and sleeps before retrying the **same credential**. With the shipped `PROVIDER_RETRY_BACKOFF_MAX_SECONDS=60` the ladder runs 2 → 4 → 8 → 16 (+1 s jitter) ≈ 32 s per key; a three-key pool spends ~100 s on those sleeps before another model is tried, while the 120 s first-token deadline keeps ticking through them.\n\nMeasured live on `nvidia_nim/moonshotai/kimi-k3`: NIM answered every attempt in 0.1 s (12×429, 3×502) and the request still took **107 s** to fall back.\n\nSeparately, a diff of `Settings.model_fields` aliases against the admin manifest keys found **4 of 263** env vars with no dashboard field at all.\n\n## Mechanism\n\nThe ceiling is a **latency budget, not a rate-limit-recovery estimate**. Every wait on the ladder is spent against one credential before routing gets a turn, so the number bounds how long a caller sits on a single key — it belongs at the scale of a request, not of an upstream window.\n\n## What this does\n\n- `PROVIDER_RETRY_BACKOFF_MAX_SECONDS` default **60 → 10** at every site that states it (`config/constants.py`, the admin manifest, README, `docs/USAGE.md`). Ladder is now 2/4/8/10, so a three-key pool reaches its chain in **≈75 s instead of ≈100 s**. Base (`2`) and jitter (`1`) unchanged; the `(0.0, HOUR)` range in `config/limits.py` unchanged; an install that already set the key is unaffected.\n- Four settings gained an admin field on the page they belong to:\n  | Env var | Page | Restart |\n  | --- | --- | --- |\n  | `WEBSEARCH_DIGEST_CHARS` | Web Search | no |\n  | `WEBSEARCH_DIGEST_CONTENT_CHARS` | Web Search | no |\n  | `WEBSEARCH_DIGEST_ANSWER` | Web Search | no |\n  | `ANTHROPIC_OAUTH_REQUIRE_CLAUDE_CODE` | Providers → Claude subscription card | **yes** |\n- `restart_required` is set from what the code does, not from a guess: the digest fields are read off a fresh `Settings()` **per request** in `api/web_tools/streaming.py` (`settings = Settings()` at the `web_search` branch), so they are not restart-gated. The OAuth gate is read **once** in `providers/runtime/factory.py` when `AnthropicOAuthProvider` is constructed, and `ProviderRuntime` caches the instance in `self._providers`, so it is.\n- The OAuth field's help text warns that turning it off routes Agent-SDK and other-harness traffic onto the subscription credential, and points at `docs/ANTHROPIC-SUBSCRIPTION.md`.\n- New `tests/contracts/test_every_setting_has_an_admin_field.py` turns the diff into a contract: every `Settings` alias must appear in `manifest.env_keys()`, with `NIM` allow-listed as a nested group (exposed as `NIM_*`), a second test naming the four recovered keys, and a third asserting the allow-list still describes a real nested model. The failure message names the missing key and the manifest file to add it to.\n\n## Verification\n\n```\nuv run ruff format          1 file reformatted, 986 files left unchanged\nuv run ruff check --fix     All checks passed!\nuv run ty check             All checks passed!\nuv run pytest -q --tb=line  15 failed, 7650 passed, 38 skipped in 123.63s\n```\n\nThe diff that motivated Part B, run against the finished branch:\n\n```\n$ uv run python -c \"...Settings.model_fields alias vs manifest.env_keys()...\"\n('nim', 'NIM', <class 'my_claude_code.config.nim.NimSettings'>)\ntotal fields 263 manifest keys 393\n```\n\n`NIM` is the nested group; nothing else is unreachable.\n\n**Pre-existing local baseline is 15 failures**, identical on unmodified `fork/main`: 8 websearch tests that read the real `~/.fcc/.env`, 6 PowerShell installer tests, and `tests/runtime/test_provider_manager.py::test_catalog_publication_tracks_warm_refresh_and_direct_cache`. GitHub runners have no `~/.fcc`, so the websearch ones pass there.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- Lowering the ceiling means a genuinely slow upstream limit is retried sooner and the pool moves to the fallback chain earlier. That is the intended trade — the chain exists for exactly this — but an operator who wants the old behaviour sets `PROVIDER_RETRY_BACKOFF_MAX_SECONDS=60` and gets it back with no code change.\n- The four new fields are wired through the generic manifest renderer and covered by the section/contract tests, but the pages were **not driven in a browser** for this change.\n- `.env.example` still names `60` in its comment: the Edit tool denies that path in this environment. No test reads the value from it, and the shipped default now comes from `config/constants.py`.\n\n## Known and deliberate (not done)\n\nThe ladder still retries the same credential before rotating, and its sleeps still count against the first-token deadline. Both are real and both are a separate change.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01RnTQRD2QEyAEcEPPahbZu6\n",
