     "date": "2026-08-30T10:24:56Z"
    },
    "message": "feat(retries): cap the retry ladder's longest wait at 10s, and expose the last four unreachable settings\n\nA single 429 could hold a request for ~100 seconds before the fallback chain\nwas ever consulted, and four env vars could only be changed by hand-editing\n~/.fcc/.env.\n\nMechanism. providers/rate_limit.py computes\n`delay = min(base * 2^attempt, max) + jitter` and sleeps before retrying the\nSAME credential. With the shipped PROVIDER_RETRY_BACKOFF_MAX_SECONDS=60 the\nladder runs 2 -> 4 -> 8 -> 16 (+1s jitter) = ~32s per key; a three-key pool\nspends ~100s on those sleeps before any other model is tried, while the 120s\nfirst-token deadline keeps ticking through them. Measured live on\nnvidia_nim/moonshotai/kimi-k3: NIM answered every attempt in 0.1s (12x429,\n3x502) and the request still took 107s to fall back. The ceiling is a latency\nbudget, not a rate-limit-recovery estimate: it bounds how long a caller sits on\none credential, so it belongs at the scale of a request, not of an upstream\nwindow.\n\nSeparately, a diff of Settings.model_fields aliases against the admin manifest\nkeys found 4 of 263 env vars with no dashboard field at all.\n\nWhat this does.\n\n- PROVIDER_RETRY_BACKOFF_MAX_SECONDS default 60 -> 10, at every site that\n  states it (constants, admin manifest, README, docs/USAGE.md). The ladder now\n  runs 2/4/8/10, so a three-key pool reaches its chain in ~=75s instead of\n  ~=100s. Base (2) and jitter (1) are unchanged, and the 0..HOUR range in\n  config/limits.py is unchanged -- an install that already set the key is\n  untouched.\n- Four settings gained an admin field on the page they belong to:\n  WEBSEARCH_DIGEST_CHARS, WEBSEARCH_DIGEST_CONTENT_CHARS and\n  WEBSEARCH_DIGEST_ANSWER on Web Search; ANTHROPIC_OAUTH_REQUIRE_CLAUDE_CODE on\n  the Claude subscription card of Providers, with the warning that turning it\n  off routes Agent-SDK and other-harness traffic onto the subscription\n  credential.\n- restart_required set from what the code does, not from a guess: the digest\n  fields are read from a fresh `Settings()` per request in\n  api/web_tools/streaming.py, so they are not restart-gated; the OAuth gate is\n  read once in providers/runtime/factory.py when the provider is constructed\n  and cached by ProviderRuntime, which owns \"one immutable settings\n  snapshot\", so it is.\n- New tests/contracts/test_every_setting_has_an_admin_field.py reproduces the\n  diff as a contract: every Settings alias must appear in\n  manifest.env_keys(), with NIM allow-listed as a nested group (it is exposed\n  as NIM_*) and a failure message that names the key and the manifest to add it\n  to.\n\nVerification.\n\n    uv run ruff format          1 file reformatted, 986 files left unchanged\n    uv run ruff check --fix     All checks passed!\n    uv run ty check             All checks passed!\n    uv run pytest -q --tb=line  15 failed, 7650 passed, 38 skipped in 123.63s\n\n    uv run python -c \"...Settings.model_fields alias vs manifest.env_keys()...\"\n    -> ('nim', 'NIM', <class ...NimSettings'>)     # the only remainder\n       total fields 263 manifest keys 393\n\nPre-existing local baseline is 15 failures, identical on unmodified fork/main:\n8 websearch tests that read the real ~/.fcc/.env, 6 PowerShell installer tests,\nand tests/runtime/test_provider_manager.py::\ntest_catalog_publication_tracks_warm_refresh_and_direct_cache.\n\nNot done. The ladder still retries the same credential before rotating, and its\nsleeps still count against the first-token deadline -- that is a separate\nchange. `.env.example` still names 60 in its comment: the Edit tool denies that\npath in this environment, and no test reads the value from it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RnTQRD2QEyAEcEPPahbZu6",
